    <bpmn:process id="W_W3538" name="W3538. Recyclable / Biodegradable Material Transition Program" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Sustainable-packaging strategy (W3526); EPR target
Frequency: Multi-year program + per-SKU transition
Volume: SKU packaging portfolio
Owner: Packaging Engineering
Participants: Packaging Eng, Merchandising (links to VS-01/VS-41), Procurement (links to VS-03/VS-34), Quality (links to VS-31), Sustainability (links to VS-25), Supplier, Marketing (links to VS-14)
Source: workflow W3538 — Recyclable / Biodegradable Material Transition Program</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3538_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3538_Lane1" name="Packaging Eng">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3538_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3538_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3538_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3538_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3538_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3538_Start3" name="Sustainable-packaging strategy (W3526); EPR target">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3538_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3538_Task4" name="Packaging Eng/Merchandising build the material-transition roadmap: SKU…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Packaging Eng/Merchandising build the material-transition roadmap: SKU prioritization (high-volume/high-plastic first), target materials (recyclable mono-material, biodegradable, compostable, recycled-content), feasibility, cost/performance trade-off, and timeline to the EPR/sustainability target (links to VS-25.3)
Responsible (R): Packaging Eng / Merchandising / Sustainability
Accountable (A): Sustainability/ESG Manager / VP Merchandising
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3538_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3538_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3538_Task5" name="Packaging Eng/Supplier develop and validate substitute packaging: spec (W3522)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Packaging Eng/Supplier develop and validate substitute packaging: spec (W3522), testing (links to VS-31), shelf-life/performance, graphics (links to VS-14), and supplier qualification; manage pilot and rollout, and last-time-buy of displaced material (links to W1026)
Responsible (R): Packaging Eng / Supplier / Quality
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Per SKU</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3538_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3538_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3538_Task6" name="Packaging Eng/FP&amp;A track transition progress (% recyclable/biodegradable…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Packaging Eng/FP&amp;A track transition progress (% recyclable/biodegradable, plastic tons reduced, cost delta), validate against the business case, and report to the ESG program (links to VS-25.3) and governance (W3544); manage trade-offs transparently
Responsible (R): Packaging Eng / FP&amp;A / Sustainability
Accountable (A): Sustainability/ESG Manager / CFO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3538_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3538_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3538_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3538_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3538_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-564 (ensure controlled execution — Packaging Sustainability, Compliance &amp; Cost Analytics (PA-111.3).) | - operational: testing and phased rollout; operational: business case and scale negotiation
Owner: Packaging Engineering</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3538_Assoc9" sourceRef="W3538_Annotation8" targetRef="W3538_Start3" associationDirection="None" />
